{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"artifacthub/community-operators/rocketmq-operator","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:16:57.691Z","source":{"name":"Artifact Hub","api":"https://artifacthub.io/api/v1/packages/olm/community-operators/rocketmq-operator","page":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/olm/community-operators/rocketmq-operator"},"readme":"The RocketMQ Operator automatically deploys and manages RocketMQ clusters on the Kubernetes-based cloud environment.\n[Apache RocketMQ](https://github.com/apache/rocketmq) is a popular distributed messaging and streaming platform with low latency, high performance and reliability, trillion-level capacity and flexible scalability.\n### Supported Features\n* **Horizontal Scaling** - Safely and seamlessly scale up each component of RocketMQ.\n* **Rolling Update** - Gracefully perform rolling updates in order with no downtime.\n* **Multi-cluster Support** - Users can deploy and manage multiple RocketMQ name server clusters and broker clusters on a single Kubernetes cluster using RocketMQ Operator.\n* **Topic Transfer** - Operator can automatically migrate a specific topic from a source broker cluster to a target cluster without affecting the business.\n### Documentation Documentation to the current _master_ branch as well as all releases can be found [here](https://github.com/apache/rocketmq-operator).","readmeBase":"https://github.com/k8s-operatorhub/community-operators/operators","publisher":{"name":"Operator Framework","url":"https://artifacthub.io/packages/search?org=operator-framework","official":false,"verified":false,"cncf":false},"registered":null,"updated":"2022-09-19T15:00:00.000Z","categories":["Streaming and messaging"],"keywords":["streaming","messaging","streams","rocketmq","midware","distributed system","Streaming & Messaging"],"license":null,"links":[{"name":"RocketMQ Documentation","url":"https://rocketmq.apache.org/"},{"name":"RocketMQ GitHub","url":"https://github.com/apache/rocketmq"},{"name":"RocketMQ Ope